    {
      "title": "Decision Trees: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Decision Trees: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Tree Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Recursive split==: one feature, one threshold at a time",
                "Leaf predicts the ==majority class== (classification)",
                "Leaf predicts the ==mean target== (regression)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Test x <= t",
                    "sub": "best split",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Recurse",
                    "sub": "each child",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Leaf",
                    "sub": "majority / mean",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. How It Grows",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Feature",
                "Split test"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Numeric",
                  "`x <= t`"
                ],
                [
                  "Categorical",
                  "subset or one-vs-rest"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Greedy} top-down: best local gain, ==no look-ahead==",
                "So the tree is **not** globally optimal",
                "No limit: splits until leaves are ==pure==",
                "Result: zero training error, {red:high variance} (overfit)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Strengths and Limits",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Strength",
                "Limit"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "No feature scaling",
                  "Axis-aligned boundaries"
                ],
                [
                  "Non-linear interactions",
                  "Unstable to small data changes"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "An unconstrained tree memorises the training set: ==0 train error==, weak test score."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why not optimal?** Greedy, no look-ahead.",
                "**Why zero training error?** Splits until leaves are pure.",
                "**Need scaling?** No, thresholds are per feature.",
                "**Why unstable?** A small data change flips an early split."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Gini vs Entropy Splits",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Gini vs Entropy Splits",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Impurity and gain",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Gini",
                "Entropy"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Formula",
                  "1 - sum(p_i^2)",
                  "-sum(p_i * log2 p_i)"
                ],
                [
                  "Pure node",
                  "0",
                  "0"
                ],
                [
                  "Balanced binary",
                  "max 0.5",
                  "max 1 bit"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Information gain== = parent impurity - **weighted average** of children's impurity",
                "The split with the {green:highest gain} wins"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Worked example",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Node: 5 ==positives==, 5 ==negatives== → Gini {blue:0.5}, entropy {blue:1.0}",
                "Split into (4,1) and (1,4): each child Gini ==0.32=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Parent (5+, 5-)",
                    "sub": "Gini 0.5",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(4,1) and (1,4)",
                    "sub": "child Gini 0.32",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Gain",
                    "sub": "0.5 - 0.32 = 0.18",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gini vs entropy",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Criterion",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Gini",
                  "cheaper (**no log**), near-identical trees"
                ],
                [
                  "Entropy",
                  "penalizes mixed nodes slightly more"
                ],
                [
                  "Regression trees",
                  "**variance (MSE) reduction** instead"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Raw gain favors ==high-cardinality== features like IDs. Use **gain ratio** or drop ID-like columns."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pruning and Controlling Tree Depth",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pruning and Controlling Tree Depth",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pre vs post pruning",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Pre-pruning== stops growth early: `max_depth`, `min_samples_split`, `min_samples_leaf`, `min_impurity_decrease`",
                "==Post-pruning== grows the full tree, then cuts weak subtrees",
                "sklearn post-pruning = cost-complexity via `ccp_alpha`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Pre-pruning",
                "Post-pruning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "{green:faster}",
                  "{red:costlier}"
                ],
                [
                  "Sees full tree",
                  "no",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "Risk",
                  "stops too early",
                  "none from stopping"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cost-complexity",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Minimize ==error + alpha * leaves==",
                "{green:Larger alpha} → smaller tree",
                "`alpha=0` → full tree kept",
                "Get candidates with `cost_complexity_pruning_path`, then cross-validate"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score",
                "path = DecisionTreeClassifier().cost_complexity_pruning_path(X, y)",
                "best = max(path.ccp_alphas, key=lambda a: cross_val_score(",
                "    DecisionTreeClassifier(ccp_alpha=a), X, y, cv=5).mean())"
              ],
              "note": "alpha picked by CV, never by the test set"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Picking alpha safely",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Pruning path",
                    "note": "candidate alphas",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cross-validate",
                    "note": "score each alpha",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Refit",
                    "note": "best alpha, all train data",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Tuning depth or alpha on the ==test set== leaks it. Tune with **CV**; touch the test set once."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bagging and Random Forests",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Bagging and Random Forests",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bagging and OOB",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Bagging==: train trees on bootstrap samples, average or vote",
                "Cuts ==variance==, bias stays the same",
                "Each bootstrap skips ~==36.8%== of rows (1/e)",
                "Those ==OOB== rows give a free score: `oob_score=True`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Random Forest vs Bagging",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Bagging",
                "Random forest"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Features per split",
                  "all p",
                  "random subset"
                ],
                [
                  "Tree correlation",
                  "high if strong features dominate",
                  "lower"
                ],
                [
                  "Ensemble variance",
                  "higher",
                  "lower"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rule of thumb `max_features`: ==sqrt(p)== classification, ==p/3== regression",
                "sklearn regressor default is `1.0` (all features): tune it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Tuning and Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`n_estimators`: more never overfits, only slower",
                "`max_features`: lower decorrelates more",
                "`min_samples_leaf`: larger smooths leaves"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Shallow trees: forests need ==deep==, low-bias trees."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does OOB work?** Each tree never saw ~36.8% of rows",
                "**Why random features?** Decorrelates trees, lowering variance",
                "**Do more trees overfit?** No, only slower"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Boosting: AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Boosting: AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Core idea",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Weak learner== = barely better than chance; ==stump== = depth-1 tree",
                "Trained ==sequentially==, each fixing the previous errors",
                "Mainly cuts {blue:bias}; bagging cuts {red:variance}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three methods",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Each round",
                "Rule"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "AdaBoost",
                  "Upweights misclassified samples",
                  "alpha = 0.5 * ln((1 - err) / err)"
                ],
                [
                  "Gradient boosting",
                  "Tree fits negative gradient (residuals for squared error)",
                  "F = F + learning_rate * tree"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**XGBoost** objective is ==regularized==: L1/L2 on leaf weights",
                "`gamma` penalty per split",
                "Second-order gradients",
                "Histogram split finding",
                "Built-in missing-value handling"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Knobs and mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Low rate, many rounds, early stop; `max_depth` 3-8, `subsample`, `colsample_bytree`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from xgboost import XGBClassifier",
                "m = XGBClassifier(learning_rate=0.05,",
                "    n_estimators=1000, max_depth=4,",
                "    subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.8,",
                "    early_stopping_rounds=50)",
                "m.fit(X_tr, y_tr, eval_set=[(X_val, y_val)])"
              ],
              "note": "fragment: X_tr, y_tr, X_val, y_val are your split"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Boosting overfits",
              "text": "Fitting residuals round after round eventually fits ==noise==. High rate or too many rounds without early stopping overfits; a forest does not."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
